<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04UZ">Remark <span data-tag="04UZ">10.2.1.15</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category, let $X$ be an object of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, and let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{0} \subseteq \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be the sieve generated by $X$ (Remark <a data-tag="04UC" href="/tag/04UC">10.2.1.14</a>): that is, the full subcategory of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ spanned by those objects $C$ for which the morphism space $\operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(C,X)$ is nonempty. Then $X$ is a subterminal object of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="04UY" href="/tag/04UY">4.7.4.1</a>) if and only if it is a final object of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{0}$ (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="02H7" href="/tag/02H7">4.7.3.1</a>). </p>
</article>
